# Content schema

Use TOML frontmatter with `+++` only (not YAML `---`).

## Paths

| Path | Kind | Required frontmatter |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `content/_index.md` | Home | `title`, `description`, `[extra]` home_* keys |
| `content/docs/_index.md` | Docs section | `title`, `description`, `sort_by = "weight"`, `template = "docs.html"`, `page_template = "doc-page.html"` |
| `content/docs/**/*.md` | Doc page | `title`, `description`, `weight` |
| `content/blog/YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md` | Blog post | `title`, `description`, `date` (only if Blog is enabled) |

Nested docs sections need their own `_index.md` with the same section fields as `content/docs/_index.md`.

## Doc page template

+++
title = "Short title"
description = "One sentence."
weight = 10
+++

## Nav

New top-level sections need a link in `[extra.devlab.navigation]` in `zola.toml`.


Do not put raw `{%` or `{{` in Markdown unless wrapped in `{% raw %}`.


After edits: `rsites check`.